mmunity, emphasizing moral conduct, the importance of the Torah, and the value of wisdom, which resonate through centuries of theological discourse. Sirach is included in the biblical canons of the Catholic and Eastern Orthodox Churches, highlighting its enduring significance in religious traditions beyond Judaism.

